Free legal aid from the Taluka Legal Services Committee (TLSC) Chevella is available to eligible individuals at the Chevella Court Premises. 
How to Apply
Physical Visit: Visit the TLSC office located within the Chevella Court Compound to meet with the Chairman (the senior-most Judge of the station) or a Panel Lawyer.
Online Application: Submit a request through the National Legal Services Authority (NALSA) Portal.
National Helpline: Dial 15100 for guidance on seeking assistance and to speak with a panel lawyer. 
Eligibility for Free Services
Free services, which cover court fees, drafting, and legal representation, are provided to:
Women and children.
Members of SC/ST communities.
Victims of trafficking or industrial workers.
Persons with disabilities.
Low-income individuals (typically earning less than ₹3,00,000 annually in Telangana). 
Services Offered
Legal Advice: Free consultation and guidance on various legal matters.
Representation: Appointment of a panel lawyer to handle cases in court at no cost to the applicant.
Documentation: Assistance with drafting petitions, affidavits, and other legal documents. 
